:169},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"0abaefb687ba0991d3255b16a8b048061318fe8b26d4b9b10ae630a8e94314f5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-rn.1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":22673},"state":{"digest":"0330c7ac132bc883b241bbc4133fbbad4ed62da5df37c827ad2d63732da39528","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-rn.1/state.json","size_bytes":183}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-rn.1","local_name":"sase-rn.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-rn","agent_clan_generation":"20260820163603","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-rn.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-rn[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Host-owned pluggable finalizer protocol[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]SASE agents finish through a beta-gated, host-owned finalizer [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]protocol in which trusted configuration activates named built-in or[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]plugin providers, `%final` selects those configured instances per [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]launch, `/sase_final` submits one atomic turn-bound declaration, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and the built-in `commit` instance preserves every current [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]attribution, publication, discarded-work, and merge-conflict [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]guarantee while requiring a reason whenever an agent refuses to [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]commit attributable repository changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]pluggable_finalizers.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/pluggable_finalizers.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-rn[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-rn/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust finalizer protocol and resolution contract[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-protocol[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-protocol: add versioned provider, instance, selector, plan, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]context, submission, result, and diagnostic wires to sase-core; own [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stable selection/dependency ordering, canonical digests, envelope [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coverage checks, and aggregate outcomes there; expose focused PyO3 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bindings and add `%final` to the shared editor directive contract; then [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]publish the core release.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the finalizer protocol core release[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-protocol[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-adopt: raise the `sase-core-rs` dependency floor, refresh the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lockfile, add the Python typed adapter and minimum-version smoke [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coverage, and keep all host-side work behind compatibility facades until[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the released binding is available.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Feature flag, repository baselines, registry, and launch [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]selection[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]host-foundation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]host-foundation: create the beta flag through `sase flag new`, capture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]late-opened repository baselines atomically, add keyed configuration and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase_finalizers` discovery with source provenance, parse ordered [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`%final` operations, reject invalid selected plans at launch, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]persist the resolved plan without changing the flag-off commit finalizer[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Turn-bound sase final declaration channel and skill[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]declaration-channel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-foundation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]declaration-channel: add `sase final context` and atomic `submit`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]opaque host-issued repository obligations, nonce and digest validation, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retained invalid-attempt diagnostics, the generated `/sase_final` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]source, and beta-only end-of-turn prompt instructions with demand-driven[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one-turn recovery and mechanical intentional-handoff exemption.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Isolated plugin and configuration finalizer execution[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]extension-runtime[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-foundation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]extension-runtime: implement the `sase_finalizers` subprocess protocol [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with sanitized environments and bounded JSON I/O, add constrained [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`builtin@command`, surface activation and provenance through `sase final[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list`, `show`, and `doctor`, and prove with a non-mutating reference [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin that installation alone never activates behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Generic controller and built-in commit parity[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]commit-reconciliation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after declaration-channel, extension-runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit-reconciliation: replace the flag-on hard-coded seam with bounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan/declare/execute/verify reconciliation, require exactly one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit-or-refuse decision per attributable dirty repository, execute [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sequential stitches through `sase stitch create`, preserve the existing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]auto-commit, publication, evidence, discard, and family rules, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retain the dedicated one-turn `--resume` conflict-repair state machine.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Compatibility migration, observability, documentation, and [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]soak gates[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]compatibility-soak[dim] · [dim][/dim]after commit-reconciliation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]compatibility-soak: map the legacy commit-finalizer settings with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]explicit diagnostics, retain compatibility artifacts and reporting, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]full flag-off/flag-on and adversarial end-to-end coverage, document the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]config/plugin/directive/CLI contracts, preview generated skill [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deployment safely, and define measurable beta-removal criteria while [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]leaving flag deletion to its dedicated flag bead.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-rn","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-rn.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-053ab21a3954ba2cf96992022462bde2","started_at":"2026-08-20T20:36:27.616729+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1787263777,"sha":"b1c6bb105fd82239c6624115ea58fa5af423657c","subject":"feat(finalizers): add beta finalizer foundati